L SUBJECTS\nL72: G. INVESTIGATOR NETWORKS TO BE INVOLVED IN THE TRIAL\nL73: N. REVIEW BY THE COMPETENT AUTHORITY OR ETHICS COMMITTEE IN THE COUNTRY CONCERNED\nL74: P. END OF TRIAL\nL75: Expand All   Collapse All\nL76: A. Protocol Information\nL77: ---\nL78: A.1  | Member State Concerned  | Spain - AEMPS\nL79: A.2  | EudraCT number  | 2015-000359-26\nL80: A.3  | Full title of the trial  |\nL81: Phase I/II safety, tolerability and initial efficacy study of adeno-associated viral vector serotype 9 containing human sulfamidase gene after intracerebroventricular administration to patients with MPSIIIA.\nL82: Estudio de fase I/II para evaluar la seguridad, tolerabilidad y eficacia inicial del vector viral adenoasociado de serotipo 9 conteniendo el gen de la sulfamidasa humana tras su administración por vía intracerebroventricular a pacientes con MPSIIIA.\nL83: A.3.1  | Title of the trial for lay people, in easily understood, i.e. non-technical, language  |\nL84: First study in patients to assess safety, tolerability and inittial efficacy of the new gene therapy product to treat MPSIIIA.\nL85: Primer estudio en pacientes para evaluar la seguridad, tolerabilidad y eficacia inicial del nuevo producto de terapia génica para tratar MPSIIIA.\nL86: A.4.1  | Sponsor's protocol code number  | ESTEVE-SANF-201\nL87: A.7  | Trial is part of a Paediatric Investigation Plan  | Yes\nL88: A.8  | EMA Decision number of Paediatric Investigation Plan  | P/149/2014\nL89: B. Sponsor Information\nL90: ---\nL91: B.Sponsor: 1\nL92: B.1.1  | Name of Sponsor  | Laboratorios del Dr. Esteve, S.A.\nL93: B.1.3.4  | Country  | Spain\nL94: B.3.1 and B.3.2  | Status of the sponsor  | Commercial\nL95: B.4 Source(s) of Monetary or Material Support for the clinical trial:\nL96: B.4.1  | Name of organisation providing support  | Laboratorios del Dr. Esteve,S.A.\nL97: B.4.2  | Country  | Spain\nL98: B.5 Contact point designated by the sponsor for further information on the trial\nL99: B.5.1  | Name of organisation  | Laboratorios del Dr. Esteve,S.A.\nL100: B.5.2  | Functional name of contact point  | Adelaida Morte\nL101: B.5.3  | Address:\nL102: B.5.3.1  | Street Address  | Av. Mare de Déu de Montserrat,221\nL103: B.5.3.2  | Town/ city  | Barcelona\nL104: B.5.3.3  | Post code  | 08041\nL105: B.5.3.4  | Country  | Spain\nL106: B.5.4  | Telephone number  | 349344660006581\nL107: B.5.6  | E-mail  | amorte@esteve.es\nL108: D. IMP Identification\nL109: ---\nL110: D.IMP: 1\nL111: D.1.2 and D.1.3  | IMP Role  | Test\nL112: D.2  | Status of the IMP to be used in the clinical trial\nL113: D.2.1  | IMP to be used in the trial has a marketing authorisation  | No\nL114: D.2.5  | The IMP has been designated in this indication as an orphan drug in the Community  | Yes\nL115: D.2.5.1  | Orphan drug designation number  | EU/3/11/877\nL116: D.3 Description of the IMP\nL117: D.3.1  | Product name  | Vector viral adenoasociado de serotipo 9 que contiene el gen de la sulfamidasa humana\nL118: D.3.2  | Product code  | AAV9-CAG-coh-SGSH\nL119: D.3.4  | Pharmaceutical form  | Suspension for injection\nL120: D.3.4.1  | Specific paediatric formulation  | No\nL121: D.3.7  | Routes of administration for this IMP  | Other use (Noncurrent)\nL122: D.3.8 to D.3.10 IMP Identification Details (Active Substances)\nL123: D.3.8  | INN - Proposed INN  | Vector viral adenoasociado de serotipo 9 que contiene el gen de la sulfamidasa humana\nL124: D.3.9.1  | CAS number  | 1352588-20-5\nL125: D.3.9.2  | Current sponsor code  | AAV9- CAG-coh-SGSH\nL126: D.3.9.3  | Other descriptive name  | Vector viral adenoasociado de serotipo 9 que contiene el gen de la sulfamidasa humana\nL127: D.3.9.4  | EV Substance Code  | SUB178857\nL128: D.3.10  | Strength\nL129: D.3.10.1  | Concentration unit  | Other\nL130: D.3.10.2  | Concentration type  | range\nL131: D.3.10.3  | Concentration number  | 1000000000000 to 1000000000000000\nL132: D.3.11 The IMP contains an:\nL133: D.3.11.1  | Active substance of chemical origin  | No\nL134: D.3.11.2  | Active substance of biological/ biotechnological origin (other than Advanced Therapy IMP (ATIMP)  | No\nL135:  | The IMP is a:\nL136: D.3.11.3  | Advanced Therapy IMP (ATIMP)  | Yes\nL137: D.3.11.3.1  | Somatic cell therapy medicinal product  | No\nL138: D.3.11.3.2  | Gene therapy medical product  | Yes\nL139: D.3.11.3.3  | Tissue Engineered Product  | No\nL140: D.3.11.3.4  | Combination ATIMP (i.e. one involving a medical device)  | No\nL141: D.3.11.3.5  | Committee on Advanced therapies (CAT) has issued a classification for this product  | No\nL142: D.3.11.4  | Combination product that includes a device, but does not involve an Advanced Therapy  | No\nL143: D.3.11.5  | Radiopharmaceutical medicinal product  | No\nL144: D.3.11.6  | Immunological medicinal product (such as vaccine, allergen, immune serum)  | No\nL145: D.3.11.7  | Plasma derived medicinal product  | No\nL146: D.3.11.8  | Extractive medicinal product  | No\nL147: D.3.11.9  | Recombinant medicinal product  | No\nL148: D.3.11.10  | Medicinal product containing genetically modified organisms  | No\nL149: D.3.11.11  | Herbal medicinal product  | No\nL150: D.3.11.12  | Homeopathic medicinal product  | No\nL151: D.3.11.13  | Another type of medicinal product  | No\nL152: D.8 Information on Placebo\nL153: ---\nL154: E. General Information on the Trial\nL155: ---\nL156: E.1 Medical condition or disease under investigation\nL157: E.1.1  | Medical condition(s) being investigated  |\nL158: Mucopolysaccharidosis type IIIA (Sanfilippo A syndrome) is an inherited lysosomal storage disease caused by a specific lysosomal enzyme deficiency that leads to intracellular accumulation of the GAG heparan sulphate (HS). It is caused by a deficiency of one of the four enzymes involved in the lysosomal degradation of HS. In the case of subtype A is the heparan N-sulfatase (SGSH).\nL159: La Mucopolisacaridosis tipo IIIA (síndrome de Sanfilippo A) es una enfermedad hereditaria de almacenamiento lisosomal causada por una deficiencia de la enzima lisosomal específica que conduce a la acumulación intracelular del Heparán Sulfato GAG (HS). Es causada por una deficiencia de una de las cuatro enzimas implicadas en la degradación lisosomal de HS. En el caso del subtipo A es el heparán N-sulfatasa (SGSH).\nL160: E.1.1.1  | Medical condition in easily understood language  |\nL161: Inherited disease caused by the deficiency of Sulfamidase, the enzime that degrades Heparan Sulfate, leading to its accumulation in the cells causing the severe signs and symptoms of MPSIIIA\nL162: Enfermedad hereditaria causada por la deficiencia de Sulfamidasa, enzima que degrada el Heparan Sulfato,conduciendo a su acumulación en las células causando los graves signos y síntomas de la MPS IIIA\nL163: E.1.1.2  | Therapeutic area  | Diseases [C] - Nutritional and Metabolic Diseases [C18]\nL164: MedDRA Classification\nL165: E.1.3  | Condition being studied is a rare disease  | Yes\nL166: E.2 Objective of the trial\nL167: E.2.1  | Main objective of the trial  |\nL168: The main objective of this study is to determine the safety and tolerability, including the immune response, after Intracerebroventricular administration of a single dose of AAV9-CAG-coh-SGSH in two dosage cohorts of patients with MPSIIIA.\nL169: El objetivo principal del estudio es determinar la seguridad y tolerabilidad, incluyendo la respuesta inmunológica, tras la administración por vía intracerebroventricular de una dosis de AAV9-CAG-coh-SGSH a dos cohortes de pacientes con MPSIIIA.\nL170: E.2.2  | Secondary objectives of the trial  |\nL171: To assess the pharmacodynamic profile and the initial efficacy after Intracerebroventricular administration of a single dose of AAV9-CAG-coh-SGSH in two dosage cohorts of patients with MPSIIIA to estimate the dose required to significantly ameliorate the phenotype.\nL172: To evaluate the correlation between the pharmacodynamic assessments and the clinical evolution, in order to establish the optimal biomarker to assess the evolution / amelioration of the disease.\nL173: To collect data regarding potential tests that can be evaluation criteria for the subsequent pivotal study.\nL174: To assess viral shedding.\nL175: Evaluar el perfil farmacodinámico y la eficacia inicial tras la administración por vía intracerebroventricular de una dosis única de AAV9-CAG-coh-SGSH a dos cohortes de pacientes con MPSIIIA para estimar la dosis requerida que mejorará significativamente el\nL176: fenotipo.\nL177: Evaluar la correlación entre la evaluación farmacodinámica y la evolución clínica de los pacientes para establecer el biomarcador óptimo que permita evaluar la evolución / mejora de la enfermedad.\nL178: Recoger datos relativos a las pruebas que potencialmente puedan constituir criterios de evaluación a ser incluidos en el subsiguiente estudio confirmatorio.\nL179: Evaluar la diseminación viral.\nL180: E.2.3  | Trial contains a sub-study  | No\nL181: E.3  | Principal inclusion criteria  |\nL182: 1.- Male and female patients aged 2 years or older.\nL183: 2.- Patients with confirmed MPSIIIA (by genotype), with underlying missense mutation at least in one of the alleles for the disease and documented deficiency in sulfamidase enzyme activity of less than or equal to 10%.\nL184: 3.- Onset of clinical manifestations related to MPSIIIA during the first 6 years of life.\nL185: 4.- Patients with an adaptive behaviour score between 40 and 90 as evaluated by the Vineland Adaptive Behaviour Scale (Vineland-II).\nL186: 5.- Patients not dependent on a wheelchair.\nL187: 6.- Patients without severe sensory deficit (blindness, deafness that requires headset).\nL188: 7.- Patients with stable symptomatic treatment (depending on weight) within the last 3 months, with no anticipated changes in medication regimen.\nL189: 8.- Patients with no contraindication for surgical procedure and/or anaesthesia. Patients taking non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs) should discontinue their use.\nL190: 9.- Patients medically stable to accommodate the protocol requirements, including travelling and assessments.\nL191: 10.- Signed informed consent.\nL192: 1.- Pacientes de ambos sexos de 2 o más años de edad.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHuidaGene Therapeutics Provides an Update on the HG302-01 First-in-Human Trial-Press release-HUIDAGENE (https://huidagene.com/new/news/82)\nciteturn677view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://huidagene.com/new/news/82\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 160\nL0: Your privacy is very important to us. When you visit our website, please agree to the use of all cookies. For more information about personal data processing, please go to 【0†Privacy Policy】.\nL1: \nL2: [Button: Accept]\nL3: \nL4:   * 【1†About】\nL5: \nL6:     * 【1†About us】\nL7:     * 【2†Leadership】\nL8:     * 【3†Investors】\nL9:     * 【4†Partnership】\nL10: \nL11:   * 【5†Science】\nL12: \nL13:     * 【5†Overview】\nL14:     * 【6†CRISPR-cas13】\nL15:     * 【7†CRISPR-cas12】\nL16:     * 【8†Scientific Publications & Presentations】\nL17: \nL18:   * 【9†Technology Platform】\nL19:     * 【9†HG-AAV Platform】\nL20:     * 【10†Animal Model Platform】\nL21:     * 【11†Manufacturing Capabilities】\nL22: \nL23:   * 【12†Pipeline】\nL24: \nL25:     * 【12†Pipeline】\nL26:     * 【13†Disease focus】\nL27: \nL28:   * 【14†Newsroom†www.huidagene.com】\nL29: \nL30:     * 【15†Press release】\nL31:     * 【16†Media】\nL32: \nL33:   * 【17†Contact us†www.huidagene.com】\nL34: \nL35:     * 【18†Get in touch】\nL36:     * 【19†Careers】\nL37: \nL38: 【20†CN†cn.huidagene.com】\nL39: \nL40: 【21†Image】 【22†Image】\nL41: \nL42: [Input: Please enter...]\nL43: \nL44: 【22†Image】\nL45: \nL46:   * #### 【1†About】\nL47: \nL48:     * ##### 【1†About us】\nL49: \nL50:     * ##### 【2†Leadership】\nL51:     * ##### 【3†Investors】\nL52: \nL53:     * ##### 【4†Partnership】\nL54: \nL55:   * #### 【5†Science】\nL56: \nL57:     * ##### 【5†Overview】\nL58: \nL59:     * ##### 【6†CRISPR-cas13】\nL60: \nL61:     * ##### 【7†CRISPR-cas12】\nL62: \nL63:     * ##### 【8†Scientific Publications & Presentations】\nL64: \nL65:   * #### 【9†Technology Platform】\nL66: \nL67:     * ##### 【9†HG-AAV Platform】\nL68: \nL69:     * ##### 【10†Animal Model Platform】\nL70: \nL71:     * ##### 【11†Manufacturing Capabilities】\nL72: \nL73:   * #### 【12†Pipeline】\nL74: \nL75:     * ##### 【12†Pipeline】\nL76: \nL77:     * ##### 【13†Disease focus】\nL78: \nL79:   * #### 【14†Newsroom†www.huidagene.com】\nL80:     * ##### 【15†Press release】\nL81: \nL82:     * ##### 【16†Media】\nL83: \nL84:   * #### 【17†Contact us†www.huidagene.com】\nL85: \nL86:     * ##### 【18†Get in touch】\nL87: \nL88:     * ##### 【19†Careers】\nL89: \nL90: 【23†Image】\nL91: \nL92: 【24†Image】\nL93: \nL94: 【15†Back to Latest News】\nL95: # HuidaGene Therapeutics Provides an Update on the HG302-01 First-in-Human Trial\nL96: \nL97: 【25†Image】\nL98: \nL99: 2026.08.05 22:00\nL100: \nL101: 【26†Image】\nL102: \nL103: Views:14249\nL104: \nL105: Follow Us on Social Media\nL106: \nL107: SHANGHAI and MIDDLETOWN, Del. | August 5, 2026 — HuidaGene Therapeutics (“HuidaGene”) today provided an update regarding a fatal serious adverse event in HG302-01, a first-in-human investigator-initiated trial evaluating HG302, an investigational gene-editing therapy for Duchenne muscular dystrophy (DMD).\nL108: This loss saddens us deeply, and we extend our heartfelt condolences to the participant's family. We are grateful for the trust placed in this research by the participant, the family, and all study participants.\nL109: In August 2025, a participant in the high-dose cohort died following administration of HG302. Because serious clinical events require careful verification of the facts and rigorous assessment of causality, HuidaGene conducted a comprehensive clinical and scientific investigation, including laboratory, immunologic, pathological, and post-mortem analyses.\nL110: Based on the available clinical and scientific evidence, the participant developed acute respiratory distress syndrome in the setting of severe complement and cytokine activation following high-dose systemic administration of an adeno-associated virus vector. The full findings of this investigation were submitted for peer review in January 2026, and additional scientific details will be shared upon publication.\nL111: The event was reported through the hospital's applicable ethics and study-oversight processes within the applicable reporting timeframe after the site became aware of it, in accordance with Good Clinical Practice. Initial and follow-up reports were subsequently submitted through those processes.\nL112: The participant was the final participant enrolled under the planned HG302-01 protocol. The other three participants did not develop the same severe clinical syndrome and remain under long-term follow-up in accordance with the study protocol.\nL113: \nL114: Patient safety is our foremost responsibility. We are committed to learning from this event, communicating validated findings responsibly, and applying those lessons to inform safer approaches for patients with serious genetic diseases.\nL115: \nL116: About HG302\nL117: HG302 is an investigational CRISPR-based gene-editing therapy designed to restore dystrophin expression in patients with DMD. HG302 has received Orphan Drug Designation from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration and was evaluated in a first-in-human clinical study.\nL118: \nL119: About Duchenne Muscular Dystrophy\nL120: Duchenne muscular dystrophy is a rare, progressive genetic disorder caused by mutations in the DMD gene, resulting in little or no functional dystrophin protein. The disease primarily affects skeletal and cardiac muscle, leading to progressive muscle weakness and functional impairment. Although available treatments can help manage symptoms and slow aspects of disease progression, none can halt or cure the disease.\nL121: \nL122: About HuidaGene\nL123: HuidaGene utilizes its proprietary AI-driven, CRISPR-based HG-PRECISE^{Ò} platform to develop potentially curative genome medicine. The company's current clinical programs include:\nL124: \nL125:   * HG004gene replacement therapy (ODD & RPDD from the US FDA and ODD from EMA) for RPE65-associated retinal disease (IRD)\nL126: \nL127:   * 'LIGHT' first-in-human trial (NCT06088992)\nL128: \nL129:   * China's first 'STAR' Phase 1/2 multi-national, \"master protocol\" clinical trial (NCT05906953)\nL130:   * HG202 CRISPR/RNA-editing therapy for neovascular age-related macular degeneration (AMD)\nL131: \nL132:   * 'SIGHT-I' first-in-human trial (NCT06031727)\nL133: \nL134:   * World's first CRISPR/RNA editing therapy 'BRIGHT' Phase 1 clinical trial (NCT06623279)\nL135: \nL136:   * HG204 RNA-editing therapy (ODD & RPDD from FDA and ODD by EMA) for MECP2 duplication syndrome\nL137: \nL138:   * World's first CRISPR/RNA-editing 'HERO' for neurodevelopment disorders first-in-human trial (NCT06615206)\nL139:   * HG302 DNA-editing therapy (ODD & RPDD from FDA) for Duchenne muscular dystrophy (DMD)\nL140: \nL141:   * World's first CRISPR/DNA-editing 'MUSCLE' first-in-human trial (NCT06594094)\nL142: The preclinical pipelines are advancing simultaneously in HG303 CRISPR/DNA-editing for ALS and CRISPR/RNA-editing therapy for Alzheimer's and Huntington's Disease. With an extensive intellectual property portfolio, HuidaGene is a leader in genome medicines for neurology and ophthalmology. Learn more at 【27†huidagene.com†www.huidagene.com】 or on 【28†LinkedIn. †www.linkedin.com】\nL143:   * 【29†Previous HuidaGene Publishes First-in-Human HG302 Study in Cell, Reporting Molecular Activity and Important Safety Findings in Duchenne Muscular Dystrophy】\nL144:   * 【30†Next HuidaGene Selected for Presidential Symposium at ASGCT 2025 Annual Meeting, Showcasing 13 Abstracts Demonstrating Breakthroughs in Gene Therapy】\nL145: \nL146: Related\nL147: recommendations\nL148:   * 【31†Dec 12,2024 HuidaGene Therapeutics Initiates M.U.S.C.L.E. Clinical Trial of HG302 for Duchenne Muscular Dystrophy and Completes First Patient Dosed】\nL149:   * 【32†Apr 11,2025 HuidaGene at CRISPR MEDiCiNE 2025: A Celebration of Progress, Promise, and Patients】\nL150:   * 【33†Nov 04,2024 HuidaGene Therapeutics Receives the First-Ever FDA Clearance of CRISPR/Cas13 RNA-Editing HG202 for Macular Degeneration】\nL151:   * 【34†Dec 06,2024 HuidaGene Therapeutics Announced First Patient Dosed in the HERO Clinical Trial of HG204 for MECP2 Duplication Syndrome】\nL152: Copyright © 2025 HuidaGene All rights reserved  【35†沪ICP备07504406号-1†beian.miit.gov.cn】  【36†沪公网安备 31011502018774号†www.beian.gov.cn】\nL153: \nL154:   * 【0†Privacy Policy】\nL155:   * 【37†Site Map】\nL156: \nL157: 【38†Image】\nL158: \nL159: 【39†Image】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMedibiofarma S.L. announced the award of the European CommissionSeal of Excellence for their clinical asset MBF-015. - Medibiofarma (https://medibiofarma.com/medibiofarma-s-l-announced-the-award-of-the-european-commissionseal-of-excellence-for-their-clinical-asset-mbf-015/)\nciteturn677view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://medibiofarma.com/medibiofarma-s-l-announced-the-award-of-the-european-commissionseal-of-excellence-for-their-clinical-asset-mbf-015/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 84\nL0: +34 948 346 255/info@medibiofarma.com\nL1: \nL2:   * 【0†Home】\nL3:   * 【1†About Us】\nL4:   * 【2†Pipeline】\nL5:   * 【3†Investors】\nL6:   * 【4†News & Events】\nL7:   * 【5†Contact】\nL8:   * 【6†Company policies】\nL9: \nL10: 【7†Image】\nL11: \nL12: News\nL13: # Medibiofarma S.L. announced the award of the European CommissionSeal of Excellence for their clinical asset MBF-015.\nL14: \nL15: Posted in\nL16: \nL17: 【8†Sin categoría】\nL18: \nL19: on\nL20: \nL21: 11 March, 2025\nL22: Navarra – February 2025 – Medibiofarma S.L., a clinical-stage biotechnology company developing\nL23: a portfolio of new small molecule therapies announced the award of the European Commission\nL24: Seal of Excellence for their clinical asset MBF-015.\nL25: The project, under the title “Re-Spark – MBF-015. A first-in-class disease-modifying therapy to\nL26: halt cognitive decline” was presented to the European Innovation Council (EIC) Accelerator\nL27: funding program and was recognised as a high-quality proposal.\nL28: MBF-015 is a patented new chemical entity which acts as an inhibitor of both HDAC1 and HDAC2\nL29: and has demonstrated synaptogenic effects in animal models. MBF-015 has recently completed a\nL30: first proof-of-concept phase IIa clinical trial in patients with Huntington’s disease where it has\nL31: demonstrated a good safety profile as well as its capacity to cross the blood brain barrier.\nL32: Richard Roberts, CSO of Medibiofarma said, “The Seal of Excellence recognizes the scientific\nL33: rationale to slow cognitive decline and the hard work of the whole team behind the development\nL34: of MBF-015. This award further confirms our commitment to advancing this project and\nL35: developing a disease-modifying treatment for Huntington’s and other neurodegenerative diseases\nL36: which patients so badly need”\nL37: About Huntington’s Disease\nL38: Huntington’s disease (HD) is an autosomal dominant neurological disease that afflicts around one\nL39: in 10,000 people. HD onset typically occurs in young adult life, and the disease is invariably fatal.\nL40: Patients initially develop small choreic movements that later intensify in amplitude and frequency,\nL41: causing an impairment of daily activities. Cognitive and psychiatric alterations are often the most\nL42: disabling symptoms for patients with HD and are among the most difficult symptoms to treat.\nL43: They are initially subtle and may go unnoticed for years but become significant later in the course\nL44: of the disease, manifesting as dementia and difficulties in executive functioning. Currently\nL45: available medications target selected symptoms, but do not provide a cure or slow its progression.\nL46: About Medibiofarma\nL47: Medibiofarma is a private biopharmaceutical company founded in 2016, devoted to the discovery\nL48: and development of new chemical entities against relevant molecular targets, with the aim of\nL49: improving the lives of patients suffering from neurological, gastrointestinal and oncological\nL50: diseases. Based on its internal capabilities in medicinal chemistry along with an experienced drug\nL51: discovery management team, Medibiofarma has developed three projects in its pipeline to early\nL52: clinical stage, in different therapeutic areas.\nL53: For more information, please visit Medibiofarma’s website (www.medibiofarma.com).\nL54: 【9†Image】\nL55: \nL56: [Input: Type your search]\nL57: #### Recent News\nL58:   * 【10†Asabys-backed Oriva Therapeutics launches to advance novel treatments for women’s health】23 January, 2026\nL59:   * 【11†Medibiofarma Successfully Completes Phase 2A Clinical Trial of MBF-118 for Fibrotic Crohn’s Disease】9 September, 2025\nL60:   * 【12†Medibiofarma Receives 2nd Funding Award from the Crohn’s & Colitis Foundation to Support Development of a New Antifibrotic Therapy】9 September, 2025\nL61:   * 【13†Palobiofarma and Medibiofarma open new headquarters in the AINbuilding in Cordovilla, Spain】11 March, 2025\nL62:   * 【14†Medibiofarma S.L. announced the award of the European CommissionSeal of Excellence for their clinical asset MBF-015.】11 March, 2025\nL63: #### Archive\nL64: \nL65:   * 【15†January 2026】\nL66:   * 【16†September 2025】\nL67:   * 【17†March 2025】\nL68:   * 【18†March 2024】\nL69:   * 【19†May 2023】\nL70:   * 【20†April 2023】\nL71:   * 【21†March 2023】\nL72:   * 【22†March 2022】\nL73:   * 【23†July 2021】\nL74:   * 【24†July 2020】\nL75:   * 【25†April 2019】\nL76:   * 【26†February 2019】\nL77:   * 【27†May 2018】\nL78: \nL79: 【28†Image: Medibiofarma】\nL80: \nL81: 【29†Priva